1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:02,980
(Mr. Huang: Thanks. That scared me)

2
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:09,700
(Delicious)

3
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,120
A yak almost charged at me yesterday.

4
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:12,080
(Complaint)
You know?

5
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:12,920
I didn't even do anything to it.

6
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:14,080
I went to take a picture with it.

7
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:15,600
I figured I'd wave at it.

8
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:16,520
I said hello.

9
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:17,380
(Just being polite)

10
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:19,120
Good thing there was a rope.

11
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:19,960
I was so scared.

12
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:24,660
(Materials sourced from the internet)

13
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:27,620
(That scared me)

14
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:28,720
What's wrong?

15
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:30,480
I went to take a picture
with a yak yesterday.

16
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:31,600
It tried to charge at me.

17
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:32,320
Really?

18
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:33,960
The smaller one.

19
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:35,040
The white one.

20
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:35,880
The big one.

21
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:36,960
Don't listen to him.

22
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:38,520
(He must've provoked it)
He was carrying beef jerky.

23
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:42,640
The yak must be wondering

24
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,920
what you were holding.

25
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,240
I saw a yak this morning.

26
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:48,000
I thought

27
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,440
about whether I could bring it down.

28
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:52,560
I was still having doubts.

29
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:54,560
Why do you keep using us as practice?

30
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:55,720
You should try practicing with it.

31
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:56,520
Get up close.

32
00:00:57,960 --> 00:00:59,400
It didn't even take half a step.

33
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:01,220
(Thankfully, I was quick)
And I jumped three or four meters away.

34
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:05,740
(Before the Singing Without Blinking game)

35
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:07,640
Your feet are pretty small.

36
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:09,960
Size 42.

37
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:10,800
(Shocked)
That big?

38
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:11,600
Size 42.

39
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:12,400
They look small.

40
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,720
I thought you were a 39.

41
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:14,720
What size are your feet, Teng?

42
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:16,360
Size 43 or 44.

43
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:17,240
Same as me.

44
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:18,240
Size 43 or 44.

45
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:20,640
Mine are bigger. Mine are a little...

46
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:22,040
(Joining the group chat)
Are your feet pretty wide?

47
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:23,400
Are your feet wide?

48
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:24,200
They're pretty thick.

49
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:25,600
They're fine. I have high arches.

50
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:26,760
With narrow shoes, I'm a 43.

51
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:28,400
Yeah.

52
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:29,400
With wide shoes, I'm a 44.

53
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:31,400
No.

54
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:32,760
I mainly look at the width.

55
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:35,760
If the width is just right, I'm a 43.

56
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:37,240
If it's a little flat...

57
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:37,960
If it's too flat, it won't work.

58
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:40,740
(Let me see)

59
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:41,680
You train hard every day.

60
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,240
(Curious)
But you don't have any calluses.

61
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:45,660
(Let me show you)

62
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:47,160
You don't have any after training.

63
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:48,240
You don't have any either.

64
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:49,180
(Let's see yours)

65
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:49,800
Look.

66
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:52,320
Now that's what you call signs of training.

67
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:53,120
You know what I mean?

68
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:54,520
I haven't done much lately.

69
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:56,520
We're the kind
who rely purely on talent.

70
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:57,600
(Talent)

71
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:59,280
We don't need
all that hard-earned experience.

72
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:02,100
(Let's check your back muscles)

73
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:05,180
(Ticklish)

74
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,640
(Curious)
What are those eye drops for?

75
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:08,880
They're for dry eyes.

76
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:10,200
(Pre-game prep)
I have to use them

77
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:11,600
before we start.

78
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:13,560
Come on.

79
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:15,080
(100% hydrated)

80
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:15,600
No, you...

81
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:16,800
(I have something to say)

82
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:19,200
You've been using eye drops for years,
haven't you?

83
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:22,040
You're so good at it.

84
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:22,880
I mean, she's not...

85
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:23,320
She's like.

86
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,280
(Who has ever seen this?)
That's some serious eyedrop skills.

87
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,040
I'm honestly amazed.

88
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:34,180
(Brainstorming a KTV argument scene)

89
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:36,120
We can only argue
on the basketball court.

90
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:37,140
(We can't even get an argument going)

91
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:40,040
What's the chorus of "I Want Freedom"?

92
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:41,400
(Another chance to show off?)

93
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,720
(Singing right away)
♪Maybe only you understand me♪

94
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:46,400
Let's do the next one together.

95
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:47,200
Sure.

96
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:48,760
(Let's set up an argument scene)
What kind of scene are we doing?

97
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:49,760
What?

98
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:50,440
(Just argue)
Just go for it.

99
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:51,500
(Got it)

100
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:53,600
(Acting)
I'm a pro at basketball and Werewolf.

101
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:54,560
Who are you to criticize me?

102
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:55,760
Playing Werewolf with you

103
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:57,280
is just like playing basketball
with you.

104
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:58,840
You'll never even see me.

105
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:00,120
I don't wanna hear it!

106
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:02,520
So it's my fault?

107
00:03:02,580 --> 00:03:03,500
(Argument over)

108
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:04,860
(Feeling the heat)

109
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:05,500
(Eye contact)

110
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:07,420
(Neither can look at the other)

111
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:11,620
(Watching the show)

112
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:13,380
Get up there
and experience it for yourself.

113
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:14,260
(You'd have to experience it
to understand)

114
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:18,240
It's like we're both holding

115
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:20,360
each other's secrets.

116
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:25,140
(Thinking about it again)

117
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:28,800
Still... still savoring the moment.

118
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:29,780
(Stop saying that)

119
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:32,120
They keep whispering to each other.

120
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:32,600
You know.

121
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,280
Watching him is making me

122
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,080
twitch.

123
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:36,760
He's opened up.

124
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:39,220
(Completely let loose)

125
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:42,220
(Casual car ride chat)

126
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:44,160
You collect postcards, right?

127
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:45,200
I collect fridge magnets.

128
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,160
(A little hobby)
I love collecting fridge magnets.

129
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,520
And the ones I like

130
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,840
are all the kind that...

131
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:50,640
Don't stick to the fridge.

132
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:52,440
The ones with unique designs.

133
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:54,520
Like those really big

134
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:55,240
buildings.

135
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:58,120
I buy those too.

136
00:03:58,120 --> 00:03:58,800
The ones featuring famous landmarks.

137
00:03:58,800 --> 00:03:59,980
(Found a shared hobby)
The iconic ones.

138
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,080
The ones with strong symbolic meaning.

139
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:01,590
Right.

140
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,720
Do you know what kind of tree this is?

141
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:08,320
A pine tree.

142
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:10,160
No.

143
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:14,600
It's a variety derived from pine trees.

144
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:15,320
(Fir)
Fir.

145
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:17,040
A fir tree.

146
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:17,960
Fir tree.

147
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:18,800
A fir tree.

148
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,800
So it grows in cold temperatures, right?

149
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:22,040
(Correct)

150
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:24,280
A fir tree that grows in cold places.

151
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:26,520
Right, on cold mountains.

152
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:27,080
"Leng shan".
[*Fir tree or cold mountain]

153
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:28,340
(A sudden bad pun)

154
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:32,120
(Cold fir tree)
A fir that grows on a cold mountain.

155
00:04:33,980 --> 00:04:35,860
(Discussion about Lin Yi's height)

156
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:37,120
Do you play sports?

157
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:38,240
No.

158
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:39,680
(He's just naturally tall)
He's just really tall.

159
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:40,720
I'm a sports college student.

160
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:41,280
A sports college.

161
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:42,840
I major in sports dance.

162
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:44,000
(What kind of dance is that?)
Sports dance?

163
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,120
It's ballroom dancing.

164
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:47,160
Latin and standard ballroom.

165
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:48,480
I thought you meant

166
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:49,920
(Running + dancing)
running while dancing.

167
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:52,000
People always assume
I'm a basketball player.

168
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:52,520
Right.

169
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,220
(Basketball Bai)
I can't play at all.

170
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:55,840
Didn't you join
the school basketball team?

171
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:56,400
I did.

172
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:58,000
(They recruited me for my height)
They made me join just because I'm tall.

173
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,080
I can't even shoot a basket.

174
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,400
You must be over 190 cm.

175
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:02,000
My actual height is 187 cm.

176
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:02,760
(How tall?)
187 cm?

177
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:03,040
No way.

178
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:03,960
Impossible.

179
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:04,320
No way.

180
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:05,040
Absolutely no way.

181
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,720
(Cheng's theory)
He wants to get cast in a romantic drama.

182
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:07,400
So he underreports his height.

183
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:07,960
You know.

184
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:10,000
I think you should add another 5 cm.

185
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,280
I think you're at least 193 cm.

186
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:12,240
Seriously?

187
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:14,840
Allen is 187 cm too.

188
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:16,000
Doesn't he seem taller than Allen?

189
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:16,680
Way taller.

190
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:18,720
I can look Allen right in the eye
when we talk.

191
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:19,680
I really thought...

192
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:20,520
When I saw him yesterday,

193
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:21,120
I was about

194
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:21,600
to talk to him.

195
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:22,040
Look at me today.

196
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:22,600
I'm wearing these really thick shoes.

197
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:23,200
Then I walked over,

198
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:24,200
and this is how I talk to him.

199
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:25,240
I'm still not as tall as he is.

200
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:28,280
These are the shoes Anyu wore yesterday.

201
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:29,800
(Enough height talk. Let's go!)
Come on, let's go.

202
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:30,800
(Materials sourced from the internet)
I measured myself in April.

203
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:32,080
(There's even a date)
Measured in April.

204
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,520
Rounded up, that's 188 cm.

205
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:37,820
(The first step to becoming an artist)

206
00:05:38,420 --> 00:05:40,460
(Daily vocal warm-up)

207
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:42,280
Everyone gets two pens.

208
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:42,920
I thought it was only me.

209
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:43,920
And I was wondering what it meant.

210
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:45,280
Oh, we've got two.

211
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:46,660
(Investigating)

212
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,880
So there's ink inside here, right?

213
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:50,020
(Shocked)
There's actually ink inside.

214
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,600
That's so fancy.

215
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:54,140
(Watch me show off my skills)

216
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:55,240
Painting with both hands.

217
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:58,000
Are there any rules
about how an artist should act?

218
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:58,680
Nope.

219
00:05:58,680 --> 00:05:59,440
Let me show you how it's done.

220
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:00,480
Which one?

221
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,720
Did you ever do your homework like this
as a kid?

222
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:09,420
(For copying practice)

223
00:06:09,420 --> 00:06:09,900
(Never used one)

224
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:13,600
When you have to write
the same character ten times.

225
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:15,060
(That's some real childhood experience)

226
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:16,560
If I begged you,

227
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:18,240
would you let me draw a mustache on you?

228
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,000
Didn't you say yours was too short?

229
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:22,400
(What a brat)
I'll draw two little curls for you.

230
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:24,000
Can you make it long or short?

231
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,240
No, you have to draw...

232
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:25,840
You have to make it...

233
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:26,880
It needs to look three-dimensional.

234
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:28,560
What you wanted to draw is flat.

235
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:30,200
Right. Give him two curled-up ends here.

236
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:30,680
Right here.

237
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:32,440
One on this side, one on the other.

238
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:34,240
Please.

239
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:35,200
Sell some rice cakes.

240
00:06:37,140 --> 00:06:39,540
(Even elimination can't stop him
from dancing)

241
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:41,200
Let's go take some photos over there.
Come on.

242
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:42,060
(An invitation)

243
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:48,260
(Now that's what I call a waterfall)

244
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:50,140
(Pulling out the phone)

245
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:51,980
(The world is full of chaos,
but taking photos brings peace)

246
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:55,260
(Lost in admiration of his own looks)

247
00:06:55,340 --> 00:06:57,780
(Fresh off the press)

248
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:59,160
Alright, let's start.

249
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:05,740
(Dance DNA activated)

250
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:09,860
(Dancing as a duo)

251
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:15,020
(You keep dancing.
I'm gonna grab a bite)

252
00:07:15,860 --> 00:07:17,180
(Keep dancing)

253
00:07:18,860 --> 00:07:21,340
(I quietly slipped away)

254
00:07:23,820 --> 00:07:26,620
(And quietly came back)

255
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:31,540
(Keep dancing)

256
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:34,140
(We're tired.
Let's just watch the waterfall)

257
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:36,740
(The birth of a little pig
on the bottom of the pot)

258
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:38,040
Sorry, Teng.

259
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:38,440
Teng.

260
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:38,840
Come on.

261
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:43,120
(The discussion is getting heated)
Is it "The Sound of Waves Remains"?

262
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:43,520
"The Sound of Waves Remains".

263
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:44,520
(Back row discussion zone & browsing zone)
That's the song, right?

264
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:45,720
(Front row discussion zone)
No, I'll listen to you guys sing it.

265
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:47,040
(Back row discussion zone)
Why does it sound like

266
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:48,800
that song from "Journey to the West"?

267
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:52,080
Isn't that a legendary song?

268
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:53,560
"The Sound of Waves Remains".

269
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:54,600
It's "The Sound of Waves Remains".

270
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:56,420
(Looking left and right)
I have no idea.

271
00:07:56,460 --> 00:07:57,660
(Heading straight for the target)

272
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:59,160
Smells good.

273
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:00,480
It must be "The Sound of Waves Remains".

274
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:02,020
(Curious)

275
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:03,500
(That's a perfect circle)

276
